    "reply": "{\n  \"claim\": \"The recovery kernel's cell grammar and rewrite execution are inconsistent for inputs containing a fenced object followed by prose or another object.\",\n  \"expected\": \"Rewrites that add or remove a trailing part should be valid when the resulting text is still a cell of the grammar, and the recovered object should remain unchanged for additions after a complete fenced object.\",\n  \"observed\": \"Several rewrites are marked INVALID_INSTANTIATION with details like 'the rewritten text is no cell of the grammar' or 'the input is not the cell it names', even when the rewritten text appears to be a valid cell; one case (fence[ A B ] with added C) unexpectedly changes the recovered object from {\\\"b\\\":2} to {\\\"c\\\":3}.\",\n  \"reproducer\": \"```\\n{\\\"a\\\": 1}\\n```\\n{\\\"b\\\": 2}\",\n  \"source_basis\": \"recover_json_object: 'Every top-level balanced object in the text is a candidate... The object scored is the last one inside a code fence when any fence holds one, else the last top-level object in the text.'\",\n  \"execution_evidence\": \"The provided test campaign results show INVALID_INSTANTIATION for proposals 3a3ffd2295cea743, ba1632743be8e4d5, d2b9bbc3bb6439e5, c883056725f16492, de585053b0a58e84, 9919b2230d4cbfc6, 604b932e83eff54f, and a moved result for 9237691326ad9586.\",\n  \"scope\": \"Recovery kernel inputs where a fenced JSON object is followed by prose or another object, and a rewrite adds or removes a trailing part.\",\n  \"uncertainty\": \"The exact grammar definition for 'cell' is not provided, so some INVALID_INSTANTIATION results may be correct if the grammar intentionally disallows certain sequences; the moved result for fence[ A B ] with added C may be intended if the last object wins, but it conflicts with the 'unchanged' expectation.\"\n}"
